---
description: "Vue 3 project standards: Reusable components, Pinia stores, Tailwind CSS, and strict TypeScript types"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Vue Project Development Rules

## Core Principles

1. **Reusability First**: Every UI element must be a reusable component
2. **Type Safety**: Everything must have proper TypeScript types - no `any` or untyped code
3. **Component Architecture**: Child components receive data from parent via props
4. **State Management**: Use Pinia for centralized state, separate stores per functionality
5. **Styling**: Use Tailwind CSS exclusively for styling

## Component Architecture

### Component Structure

- **Never use built-in HTML elements directly** - Always create custom components
- **Generic/Reusable Components**: Create generic components for common UI patterns
- **Child Components**: All components should be child components that receive data via props
- **No direct API calls in components**: Components receive data from parent or Pinia stores

### Required Generic Components

**CRITICAL**: Every UI element must be a reusable generic component. Never create one-off components or use built-in HTML elements directly.

Create these reusable components in `src/components/generic/`:

1. **Table Component** (`GenericTable.vue`)
   - Accepts: columns, data, loading state via props
   - Handles: sorting, row selection
   - **Note**: Does NOT handle pagination - use GenericPagination separately
   - Type: Generic with TypeScript generics for type safety
   - **Must be reusable** for all table displays across the app

2. **Pagination Component** (`GenericPagination.vue`)
   - Accepts: currentPage, totalPages, totalItems, itemsPerPage, loading via props
   - Handles: page navigation, items per page selection
   - Emits: page-change, items-per-page-change events
   - **Must be used everywhere pagination is needed** - never create custom pagination
   - Works with PaginatedResponse type from API
   - Fully reusable across all features (products, orders, users, etc.)

3. **Card Component** (`GenericCard.vue`)
   - Accepts: title, content, actions, variant via props
   - Reusable for all card displays across the entire application
   - Never create feature-specific card components

4. **Button Component** (`GenericButton.vue`)
   - Accepts: variant, size, loading, disabled, icon via props
   - Handles all button styles and states
   - **Must replace all `<button>` elements** in the application

5. **Paragraph/Text Component** (`GenericText.vue`)
   - Accepts: variant, size, weight, color via props
   - **Must replace all `<p>`, `<span>`, `<h1-h6>` elements**
   - Single source of truth for all text styling

6. **Input Component** (`GenericInput.vue`)
   - Accepts: type, label, placeholder, error, validation via props
   - Handles all form inputs
   - **Must replace all `<input>`, `<textarea>`, `<select>` elements**

7. **Modal/Dialog Component** (`GenericModal.vue`)
   - Accepts: isOpen, title, content, actions via props
   - Reusable for all modals across the application
   - Never create custom modal implementations

### Component Rules

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Generic reusable component
<script setup lang="ts">
interface Props {
  data: TableData[];
  columns: Column[];
  loading?: boolean;
}
const props = defineProps<Props>();
</script>

// ❌ WRONG: Using built-in elements directly
<div>...</div> // Don't use raw HTML elements

// ❌ WRONG: Component making API calls
const response = await fetch('/api/data'); // Don't do this in components
```

## TypeScript Standards

### Type Requirements

- **No `any` types** - Everything must have explicit types
- **API Response Types**: Every API response must have a defined interface/type
- **Props Types**: All component props must be typed with interfaces
- **Store Types**: All Pinia store state, getters, and actions must be typed
- **Event Types**: All emitted events must have typed payloads

### Type Examples

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Properly typed API response
interface ApiResponse<T> {
  data: T;
  message: string;
  status: number;
}

interface UserResponse extends ApiResponse<User> {}

// ✅ CORRECT: Typed component props
interface ButtonProps {
  variant: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'danger';
  size: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg';
  disabled?: boolean;
  loading?: boolean;
}

// ❌ WRONG: Untyped or any
const data: any = ...; // Never use any
const response = await api.get('/users'); // Must type the response
```

## Pinia Store Management

### Store Structure

- **One store per functionality/feature**
- **Centralized state management** - No component-level state for shared data
- **Typed stores**: All stores must have proper TypeScript types

### Store Organization

```
src/stores/
  ├── auth.store.ts      # Authentication state
  ├── user.store.ts      # User management
  ├── product.store.ts   # Product management
  ├── order.store.ts     # Order management
  └── ...
```

### Store Rules

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Typed Pinia store with pagination
import { defineStore } from 'pinia';
import type { PaginatedResponse, PaginationMeta } from '@/types/api.types';

interface UserState {
  users: User[];
  currentUser: User | null;
  pagination: PaginationMeta | null; // Required for paginated endpoints
  loading: boolean;
}

export const useUserStore = defineStore('user', {
  state: (): UserState => ({
    users: [],
    currentUser: null,
    pagination: null, // Store pagination metadata
    loading: false,
  }),
  getters: {
    activeUsers: (state): User[] => {
      return state.users.filter(u => u.isActive);
    },
  },
  actions: {
    // For paginated endpoints - MUST use PaginatedResponse
    async fetchUsers(page: number = 1, limit: number = 10): Promise<void> {
      this.loading = true;
      const response: PaginatedResponse<User> = await api.get(`/users?page=${page}&limit=${limit}`);
      this.users = response.data;
      this.pagination = response.pagination; // Store pagination metadata
      this.loading = false;
    },
    // For non-paginated endpoints
    async fetchCurrentUser(): Promise<void> {
      const response: ApiResponse<User> = await api.get('/users/me');
      this.currentUser = response.data;
    },
  },
});

// ❌ WRONG: Untyped store, missing pagination, or component-level API calls
const users = ref([]); // Don't use component state for shared data
const response = await api.get('/users'); // Must type as PaginatedResponse<User>
// Missing pagination state for paginated endpoints
```

## Data Flow Pattern

### Component Data Flow

```
Parent Component
  ↓ (passes data via props)
Child Component (GenericTable, GenericCard, etc.)
  ↓ (emits events)
Parent Component
  ↓ (calls Pinia store action)
Pinia Store
  ↓ (makes API call)
API
```

### Example Pattern

```vue
<!-- ParentComponent.vue -->
<script setup lang="ts">
import { useProductStore } from '@/stores/product.store';
import GenericTable from '@/components/generic/GenericTable.vue';
import GenericPagination from '@/components/generic/GenericPagination.vue';

const productStore = useProductStore();

onMounted(() => {
  productStore.fetchProducts(1);
});

const handlePageChange = (page: number) => {
  productStore.fetchProducts(page);
};

const handleItemsPerPageChange = (itemsPerPage: number) => {
  productStore.setItemsPerPage(itemsPerPage);
  productStore.fetchProducts(1);
};
</script>

<template>
  <div>
    <!-- Always use GenericTable - never create custom tables -->
    <GenericTable
      :data="productStore.products"
      :columns="tableColumns"
      :loading="productStore.loading"
      @row-click="handleRowClick"
    />
    
    <!-- Always use GenericPagination - never create custom pagination -->
    <GenericPagination
      v-if="productStore.pagination"
      :current-page="productStore.pagination.page"
      :total-pages="productStore.pagination.totalPages"
      :total-items="productStore.pagination.total"
      :items-per-page="productStore.pagination.limit"
      :loading="productStore.loading"
      @page-change="handlePageChange"
      @items-per-page-change="handleItemsPerPageChange"
    />
  </div>
</template>
```

## Tailwind CSS Usage

### Styling Rules

- **Use Tailwind classes exclusively** - No inline styles or CSS files
- **Create reusable utility classes** if needed (via Tailwind config)
- **Component variants** should use Tailwind classes via computed props

```vue
<!-- ✅ CORRECT: Using Tailwind -->
<button :class="[
  'px-4 py-2 rounded',
  variant === 'primary' ? 'bg-blue-500 text-white' : 'bg-gray-200',
  disabled && 'opacity-50 cursor-not-allowed'
]">

<!-- ❌ WRONG: Inline styles or CSS files -->
<button style="padding: 10px; background: blue;">
```

## File Organization

### Component Structure

```
src/
  ├── components/
  │   ├── generic/          # Reusable generic components
  │   │   ├── GenericTable.vue
  │   │   ├── GenericCard.vue
  │   │   ├── GenericButton.vue
  │   │   ├── GenericText.vue
  │   │   └── GenericInput.vue
  │   └── feature/          # Feature-specific components
  │       ├── ProductCard.vue
  │       └── OrderList.vue
  ├── stores/               # Pinia stores (one per feature)
  ├── types/                # TypeScript type definitions
  │   ├── api.types.ts      # API response types
  │   ├── component.types.ts # Component prop types
  │   └── entity.types.ts   # Entity types
  └── views/                # Page components
```

## API Integration

### API Type Requirements

```typescript
// types/api.types.ts
export interface ApiResponse<T> {
  data: T;
  message: string;
  status: number;
  errors?: string[];
}

// Pagination metadata - used by GenericPagination component
export interface PaginationMeta {
  page: number;
  limit: number;
  total: number;
  totalPages: number;
}

// Paginated response - MUST be used for all paginated API endpoints
export interface PaginatedResponse<T> extends ApiResponse<T[]> {
  pagination: PaginationMeta;
}

// All API calls must return typed responses
async function fetchUsers(page: number = 1): Promise<PaginatedResponse<User>> {
  const response = await api.get(`/users?page=${page}`);
  return response as PaginatedResponse<User>;
}

// Store must use PaginatedResponse type
interface UserState {
  users: User[];
  pagination: PaginationMeta | null;
  loading: boolean;
}
```

### Pagination Integration Pattern

**CRITICAL**: All paginated data must use `PaginatedResponse<T>` type and `GenericPagination` component.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Using PaginatedResponse and GenericPagination
const productStore = useProductStore();
await productStore.fetchProducts(1); // Returns PaginatedResponse<Product>

// In component
<GenericPagination
  :current-page="productStore.pagination?.page || 1"
  :total-pages="productStore.pagination?.totalPages || 0"
  :total-items="productStore.pagination?.total || 0"
  :items-per-page="productStore.pagination?.limit || 10"
  :loading="productStore.loading"
  @page-change="productStore.fetchProducts"
  @items-per-page-change="handleItemsPerPageChange"
/>

// ❌ WRONG: Custom pagination or untyped response
<div class="pagination">...</div> // Never create custom pagination
const response = await api.get('/users'); // Must use PaginatedResponse type
```

## Component Communication

### Props and Events

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Typed props and events
interface Props {
  items: Item[];
  selectedId?: string;
}

interface Emits {
  (e: 'select', id: string): void;
  (e: 'update', item: Item): void;
}

const props = defineProps<Props>();
const emit = defineEmits<Emits>();
```

## Reusability Requirements

### Core Principle: Everything Must Be Reusable

**Before creating any component, ask:**
1. Can this be made generic and reusable?
2. Will other features need similar functionality?
3. Can I use an existing generic component instead?

**Rules:**
- ✅ **DO**: Create generic components that work across all features
- ✅ **DO**: Use existing generic components (GenericTable, GenericPagination, GenericCard, etc.)
- ❌ **DON'T**: Create feature-specific components when a generic one can work
- ❌ **DON'T**: Duplicate pagination, table, or card logic
- ❌ **DON'T**: Use built-in HTML elements directly

### Generic Component Usage Examples

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Using GenericPagination everywhere
// Products page
<GenericPagination :current-page="productStore.pagination.page" ... />

// Orders page  
<GenericPagination :current-page="orderStore.pagination.page" ... />

// Users page
<GenericPagination :current-page="userStore.pagination.page" ... />

// ❌ WRONG: Creating custom pagination for each feature
<div class="product-pagination">...</div> // Don't do this
<div class="order-pagination">...</div>   // Don't do this
```

## Checklist for New Components

- [ ] Component is generic and reusable across multiple features
- [ ] Checked if existing generic component can be used instead
- [ ] All props are typed with interfaces
- [ ] All events are typed
- [ ] Uses Tailwind CSS for styling
- [ ] Receives data from parent or Pinia store
- [ ] No direct API calls in component
- [ ] No `any` types used
- [ ] Follows naming convention (GenericXxx.vue for reusable components)
- [ ] If pagination is needed, uses GenericPagination component
- [ ] If table is needed, uses GenericTable component
- [ ] If card is needed, uses GenericCard component

## Checklist for New Stores

- [ ] Store is typed (state, getters, actions)
- [ ] One store per functionality
- [ ] API responses are typed (use PaginatedResponse<T> for paginated endpoints)
- [ ] Pagination metadata is stored in state when using paginated endpoints
- [ ] Actions return typed promises
- [ ] No `any` types used
- [ ] Pagination state follows PaginationMeta interface structure

## Examples

### Generic Table Component

```vue
<!-- GenericTable.vue -->
<script setup lang="ts" generic="T">
interface Column<T> {
  key: keyof T;
  label: string;
  sortable?: boolean;
}

interface Props<T> {
  data: T[];
  columns: Column<T>[];
  loading?: boolean;
}

const props = defineProps<Props<T>>();
</script>
```

### Generic Pagination Component

```vue
<!-- GenericPagination.vue -->
<script setup lang="ts">
interface Props {
  currentPage: number;
  totalPages: number;
  totalItems: number;
  itemsPerPage: number;
  loading?: boolean;
}

interface Emits {
  (e: 'page-change', page: number): void;
  (e: 'items-per-page-change', itemsPerPage: number): void;
}

const props = defineProps<Props>();
const emit = defineEmits<Emits>();

const handlePageChange = (page: number) => {
  emit('page-change', page);
};

const handleItemsPerPageChange = (itemsPerPage: number) => {
  emit('items-per-page-change', itemsPerPage);
};
</script>

<template>
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
    <!-- Pagination controls -->
    <div class="flex gap-2">
      <GenericButton
        :disabled="currentPage === 1 || loading"
        @click="handlePageChange(currentPage - 1)"
      >
        Previous
      </GenericButton>
      <GenericText>{{ currentPage }} of {{ totalPages }}</GenericText>
      <GenericButton
        :disabled="currentPage === totalPages || loading"
        @click="handlePageChange(currentPage + 1)"
      >
        Next
      </GenericButton>
    </div>
    <!-- Items per page selector -->
    <GenericInput
      type="select"
      :value="itemsPerPage"
      @change="handleItemsPerPageChange"
    />
  </div>
</template>
```

### Typed Store Usage

```typescript
// In component
const productStore = useProductStore();
const products: Product[] = productStore.products; // Typed
await productStore.fetchProducts(); // Returns Promise<void>
```

